Newspeak3
'Newspeak'
class AsyncBridgeProbeApp packageUsing: manifest = Object new (
	(* Deployable wrapper so AsyncBridgeProbe can run headlessly.

 The probe needs a live JS side — js global, setTimeout, Promise, JSON — and the
 native primordialsoup VM has none: primitives.cc guards JS_pushValue and its
 siblings with `#if !defined(OS_EMSCRIPTEN) return kFailure;`. So there is no
 command-line shortcut for the psoup half; it has to be the WASM build in a page.

 Build (from the directory the static server serves, with AsyncBridgeProbe.ns
 and this file copied in):

   $PRIMORDIALSOUP/out/ReleaseX64/primordialsoup \
     $PRIMORDIALSOUP/out/snapshots/WebCompiler.vfuel \
     ./*.ns ./*.png RuntimeForHopscotchForHTML AsyncBridgeProbeApp AsyncBridgeProbe.vfuel

 Run:  primordialsoup.html?snapshot=AsyncBridgeProbe.vfuel — results arrive as
 console lines, which a CDP driver collects as Runtime.consoleAPICalled events.

 The same probe module is what the NS→JS deploy should run, so the two runtimes
 are compared on identical code. *)
	
	|
		private AsyncBridgeProbe = manifest AsyncBridgeProbe.
	|
) (
	public main: platform args: args = (
		(* No UI: the probe reports to console, which is all a headless driver can
   read anyway. Nothing is retained from the manifest beyond the class
   extracted at initialization. *)
		
		(AsyncBridgeProbe usingPlatform: platform) runAllToConsole
	)
) : ()
